A||||10||80's BOY||a challenge for the best of Fiero experts||||3||
Z||000000||80's BOY||04-05-2000||02:33 PM||||now that i've got your attention...<BR>I'm working on a full targa kit for my 1985 GT. i just can't make myself cut the top out without finding SOMEONE who has at least tried to do this before. my car is show quality so far, so this will not be a crap job. frame reinforcements will be implemented. that means more weight. if i cut out the top and replace the roof frame with two large round pipes or bars between the front and rear area above your head, and then make some nice padded leather covers for them and the remaining area above the sun visors, this could serve as a cushion for the top when it is latched on again using varios roof seals which will be special ordered from a local body shop. this kit will mimic a factory Honda del-sol with a front seal from perhaps a convertible sun-bird or similar car. any suggestions/ideas on this project?? it is a weekend show car that only comes out in the sunshine and sleeps all week. help me let the sun in!!!||||reg||3
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-05-2000||03:29 PM||||Not sure how the canvertable lambo kits do it but if the heavyer lambo doors, and body cladding can be supported by the stock fram I'm sure your lightly modified body will do ok with what you have sugested.. I had an 87 Supra Turbo.. it was a Targa.. might want to look in to getting a roof from one of them and grafting it in place...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||04-05-2000||03:39 PM||||Corson Motor Cars used to make a targa kit, maybe still do.<BR>It is basically t-tops without the center bar and one removable fiberglass top portion.  They used an x frame underneath for strength. <BR>FYI: The front part of the Sunbird frame does fit the Fieros front.<BR>Also, make sure you have the X frame mounted before you cut the top out.<BR>Corson: (602) 375-2544||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||04-05-2000||04:59 PM||||On my Lambo kit I welded 2x2 steel tubing in the door frames 11" up from the bottom but that wouldn't be an option for your car. I drove the frame around on some bumpy roads and none of my measurments changed. You will need some support if you cut the roof structure||||reg||1
Z||000004||80's BOY||04-05-2000||10:05 PM||||also some people have told me to be sure to jack the car up from the center with two floor jacks, then cut the roof and weld the support. makes sense to me. someone else told me that they welded larger steel pipe where the existing coolant tubes run under the chassis, thus increasing stability AND supplying greater cooling capabilities due to the larger diameter cooling pipes. or maybe an X frame will do just fine. has anyone ever changed their fuel pump from the inside of the car by cutting an access hole?? this is a big concern.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000005||DJRice||04-06-2000||09:12 AM||||I think youd have to cut a big hole for that or else cut the fuel lines and replace them with rubber hose.  Fuel lines attached to the pump assy are metal tubing and as I recall are 18-24 inches long.  I guess its not that big of a deal tho, if your willing to cut through the body to get to it from the top.  I would definitely take the gas tank out first, then cut the hole.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spyder||04-06-2000||10:09 AM||||The fuel pump was my concern at one time, so I installed an external fuel pump. You can leave the old pump in and the fuel will flow through it. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||80's BOY||04-06-2000||10:50 AM||||i assume you just disconnected the factory fuel pump. i was told there would be too much restriction from leaving it. also where did you install the new one?? maybe where the lines connect going up to the fuel rail in the engine bay?? how large of a pump??||||reg||5
Z||000008||80's BOY||04-06-2000||10:52 AM||||is 602-375-2544 the only number to Corson Motor Cars?? this is a fax only number. are they reliable??||||reg||1
Z||000009||88 Fiero||04-06-2000||12:15 PM||||I ran into a website of a guy that have a 355 Kit on his Fiero with a Targa Top. He said that he uses the Corvette Assemby for this Targa. and the top is made of vinyl with a piano hinge?? on it so he can fold it in half and store it away. He did not indicate where to store. But he said it works.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Spyder||04-08-2000||12:01 AM||||I just disconnected the factory pump and left it there, I’m using the Holley external fuel pump, but I have a V8 with a carburetor.  So I didn’t need as much pressure. I actually have too much pressure so I’m having to install a smaller pump. <P><BR>Here is the Corson web site:<BR>They have been around a long time. <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/corson.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/corson.html</A> <P>Here is the link to the picture of my engine with the fuel pump on the bottom left of the pic. <A HREF="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/motorin.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.markalexandermiller.com/motorin.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
